   username (accepted as provided, never "verified") and skills. #2 extends the
   developer profile into the portfolio (URLs, availability).
 
+## Decisions of 30 Oct 2026 (#2 implementation, for review)
+
+- **Portfolio = the onboarding profile, extended.** Headline, bio, GitHub
+  username and skills come from #1 and stay editable; #2 adds project links,
+  a resume link and "Available for work". The GitHub *username* is kept (shown
+  as a link to `github.com/<username>`) rather than asking for a URL.
+- **Projects:** up to 6, each a title (≤ 80), a repository link (required) and
+  a live-demo link (optional). Links: `http`/`https`, a host with a dot, ≤ 200
+  characters, accepted as entered; nothing is labelled or described as verified.
